  "body": "### Description\r\n\r\nI sent an ACL to deny matrix.org, and this ended up banning all servers from participating. It seems to cause \"allow: []\" to get added to the event, which causes every server to be banned. \r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\nIn Riot, I sent the following state event from dev tools:\r\n\r\n```\r\n{\r\n    \"content\": {\r\n        \"allow\": [\r\n            \"*\"\r\n        ],\r\n        \"allow_ip_literals\": false,\r\n        \"deny\": [\r\n            \"matrix.org\"\r\n        ]\r\n    },\r\n    \"type\": \"m.room.server_acl\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nI then see the following in the chat in Riot: \"<me> set server ACLs for this room: 🎉 All servers are banned from participating! This room can no longer be used.\"\r\n\r\nIf I look at the m.room.server_acl in dev tools, I see this:\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"type\": \"m.room.server_acl\",\r\n  \"sender\": \"<my mxid>\",\r\n  \"content\": {\r\n    \"content\": {\r\n      \"allow\": [\r\n        \"*\"\r\n      ],\r\n      \"allow_ip_literals\": false,\r\n      \"deny\": [\r\n        \"matrix.org\"\r\n      ]\r\n    },\r\n    \"type\": \"m.room.server_acl\",\r\n    \"allow\": []\r\n  },\r\n  \"state_key\": \"\",\r\n  \"origin_server_ts\": 1560649579360,\r\n  \"unsigned\": {\r\n    \"age\": 80\r\n  },\r\n  \"event_id\": \"<event_id>\",\r\n  \"room_id\": \"<room_id>\"\r\n}\r\n```\r\n(note the \"\"allow\": []\" added into the acl.) \r\n\r\n### Version information\r\n\r\nThis is happening on a self-hosted synapse 1.0. I am able to reproduce this in a new room every time. \r\n",
